        "@value": "Uniquely identifies an external element."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/analysis",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual",
      "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Analytical evaluating of data, designs, or processes methodically to verify correctness against standards or expectations. Typical analysis methods are FMEA, FTA, STPA, static analysis for MISRA compliance etc."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "analysis"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/RelationshipType/follows",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual",
      "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/RelationshipType"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The `to` Element succeeds the `from` Element, establishing a unidirectional sequence. This succession is defined as chronological, procedural, or logical. It is used to represent either a temporal order (e.g., in a workflow) or a logical order for processing and traversal (e.g., in an ordered list)."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "follows"
      }
    ]
  },
